A||||3||mshill||Need help removing doors w/power acc.||||1||
Z||000000||mshill||01-30-2001||03:29 PM||||I need to remove my doors which is usually pretty easy, however, my doors have power everything.  Should I disconnect the accessory connections in the door or is there a single connector inside the car that disconnects everything?  Does all the wiring remain attached to the door or to the car?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Tigger||01-30-2001||03:38 PM||||I believe there's a plug in the corner footwell, you'll need to pull the carpet back.  The wide plug is for pwr windows and locks.  Also there should be a seperate small plug for the mirrors.  That's the quickest way to disconnect everything.  The wiring from there can be removed competely with the door on or off the car.<P>Use two flat screwdrivers or something with a flat U shape to pop those plastic wire clips from the door inner.  I know a couple are a pain.<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 01-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||01-30-2001||07:20 PM||||there are 2or3 connectors inside the car under the carpet on each side. These must be unplugged and the rubber boot shoved out of the hole before the door is removed.||||reg||1
Z||000003||mshill||01-30-2001||11:56 PM||||Thanks guys.  Same day service.  I love this place.<BR>||||reg||1
